# i18n

- Locales `en` (default) and `pt`; BCP-47 `pt-BR` for `<html lang>`, hreflang and `Intl`, `pt_BR` for Open Graph (`localeTags`, `ogLocales` in `src/i18n/routing.ts`).
- No hard-coded user-facing string in public components: text, `aria-label`, `alt`, tooltips, toasts and terminal output all come from `messages/{en,pt}.json` via `next-intl`. Exceptions: the admin UI (English only) and the lazy secret-command module.
- Proper nouns (owner name, technology names) are not translated.
- Add every key to both files in the same commit. Write Portuguese natively (first person, natural syntax, keep terms like deploy, backend, framework, pipeline, commit), never as a literal translation. No exclamation marks, no emoji, sentence case.
- Content from the repository arrives already resolved to one locale; components never receive `{ en, pt }` objects.
- Format dates, numbers and lists with `Intl` / next-intl formatters.
- Locale resolution uses `next/root-params` (`src/i18n/request.ts`); do not use `setRequestLocale`. Server Actions and Route Handlers cannot read root params: pass the locale explicitly.
- Only `/` negotiates a locale (proxy). The `NEXT_LOCALE` cookie is written only on an explicit switch (`saveLocalePreference`).
